{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Arthur awoke to the distinct sound of a loading screen. Blinking, he sat up in his bed, the familiar floral wallpaper suddenly… pixelated. His room wasn't his room. It was a brightly colored, overly-stylized chamber with impossible angles and furniture that seemed to defy gravity. A digital sun shone through a window that displayed a sky rendered in vibrant, unnatural hues. He reached out to touch the bedside table, and his hand passed right through it. Panic flared as he realized the floral wallpaper wasn’t wallpaper at all, but a texture, a visual effect within a larger, coded environment. He scrambled out of bed, his movements jerky and unnatural, like a character in a poorly optimized game. A notification popped up in his vision – \"Player Arthur, Level 1 Initiated.\"\n\n***\n\nHe stumbled out of the room and into a bustling marketplace, populated by strangely dressed people with exaggerated features. Every interaction felt scripted, every conversation delivered in pre-programmed lines. A vendor offered him a shimmering, glowing apple, and Arthur instinctively knew it was a quest item. He tried to ask the vendor what a quest was, but the vendor simply repeated, \"Quest: Obtain Golden Acorn. Location: Whispering Woods.\" Arthur felt a wave of nausea wash over him. He wasn’t just dreaming; he was trapped, a character in someone else’s elaborate, meticulously crafted world. The realization hit him with the force of a game crash – he was inside a video game, and he had no idea how to get out.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.7354406118392944}, {"token": "▁awoke", "logprob": -0.5083379745483398}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.003836772171780467}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.007919815368950367}, {"token": "▁distinct", "logprob": -2.120065212249756}, {"token": "▁sound", "logprob": -0.27963536977767944}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob"